Fix a soundness bug: an extreme (`least`/`greatest`) predicate may not quantify over a type as large as the ordinals, but the check looked only at the bound variable's type arguments. It now also looks inside datatype and codatatype fields, and rejects ranging over the whole of a type whose definition is not visible — a type parameter, an abstract type, or a type hidden by an export set — since that could involve an `ORDINAL` too. Quantification confined to a finite range is still allowed, as is a lambda parameter or a finite comprehension's bound variable
